===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Of [[before-and-after]] [[image]]s: the one that shows the difference before a specified treatment.
#: {{cot|en|after#Noun}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1918|month=April|title=Before and After|editor=Arthur Deerin Call|journal=Advocate of Peace|volume=LXXX|issue=4|location=Washington, D.C.|publisher=w:American Peace Society|section=“Editorial Notes” section|page=105|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/sim_world-affairs-us_1918-04_80_4/page/105/mode/1up|column=2|issn=2155-7799|oclc=6797409|passage=On the left of the double column of photographs are the “'''befores'''.” Look at them! Fine boys all, yet here is an unformed mouth; there, a fine face just missing strength by a slight over-plumpness of feature; below, a clever face just a shade too “smart”; on the next page, a form too slight and beginning to stoop. On the right are the “afters.”}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1973|author=w:Mary Lutyens|chapter=8|title=Cleo|location=London|publisher=[[w:Michael Joseph (publisher)|Michael Joseph]]|page=164|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/cleo0000luty/page/164/mode/1up|isbn=0 7181 1138 9|passage=I told them that I was taking part in a ‘Before and After’ feature for the magazine. The beauty editor had picked a couple of girls in the office to experiment on. ‘I always think that the '''befores''' look better than the afters in that kind of experiment,’ Aunt G said.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2017|author=Meagan Cass|chapter=Calling All Soloflex Men|title=ActivAmerica|location=Denton, Tex.|publisher=w:University of North Texas Press|page=100|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/activamerica0000cass/page/100/mode/1up|isbn=9781574416947|passage=Sometimes we’d agree the person looked better in their '''before'''. Happier somehow. More themselves before the muscles. {{...}} Other times we’d laugh at the '''befores'''. I’d make a crack, something like, “People should need a special government ID to buy spandex like that. It’s a question of public safety.”}}
# {{lb|en|uncommon|often|poetic}} That which occurred or existed previously.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1982|author=w:Hugh Seidman|chapter=Hymn|title=Throne/Falcon/Eye: Poems|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher=w:Random House|isbn=9780394525099|newversion=quoted in|2ndauthor=[[w:Michael Heller (poet)|Michael Heller]]|entry2=SEIDMAN, Hugh|editors2=James Vinson; D{{quote-gloss|aniel}} L{{quote-gloss|ane}} Kirkpatrick|title2=Contemporary Poets|series2=Contemporary Writers of the English Language|edition2=4th|location2=New York, N.Y.|publisher2=[[w:St. Martin's Press|St. Martin’s Press]]|year2=1985|pages2=763–764|pageurl2=https://archive.org/details/contemporarypoet00dict/page/763/mode/1up|isbn2=0-312-16837-3|passage=As all are commanded to yield like the mummy when the dung beetle rolls the sun / before all the '''befores''' of the trillion nights past night and day / though I knew that the broken receding mouth of the Sphinx had nothing to add / of resurrection in the history of its grimace.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1995|author=w:Maria Luisa Spaziani|chapter_tlr=Laura Stortoni|chapter=The Aegean|title=Sentry Towers|location=Berkeley, Calif.|publisher=Hesperia Press|page=41|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/sentrytowers00spazrich/page/41/mode/1up|isbn=0-9641003-1-2|passage=Your music has lasted since the beginning of the world. A stone was born in the waters. {{...}} Voice rising to heaven, pure music, green primal root, mother-sea, before all the '''befores'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1998|author=w:Janice Kulyk Keefer|chapter=Prologue: A Bridge of Words|title=Honey and Ashes: A Story of Family|location=Toronto, Ont.|publisher=[[w:Harper Perennial|HarperPerennialCanada]]|page=3|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/honeyashesstoryo0000keef/page/3/mode/1up|isbn=0-00-648504-9|passage=Yet when I was a child, I stood with my mother on that distant shore, or walked with her up the road, past orchards of plums and pears, past fields narrow as piano keys. To the village where she was born, and her mother before her; all other mothers, all the '''befores''' that ever were.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2000|author=Daniel Villasenor|chapter=6|title=The Lake|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher=[[w:Viking Press|Viking]]|page=30|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/lakenovel0000vill/page/30/mode/1up|isbn=0-670-89161-4|passage=Because we’re in debt to that '''before''', to all the '''befores''' where the life was before the words. Every time we pick up a hammer and a nail there’s a dead man in it who built a lean-to out of the weather in Wyoming in December or a farmer in Latin America someplace on the back of a mule-drawn cart broken down with a town’s vegetables rotting in the sun or a Mennonite right over there in McGaheysville this minute saying no to some nigh useless particle board siding and still fashioning his house with his hand.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2001|author=Ezra Scott|chapter=Anavak’s Tale|title=Angel Up My Sleeve|location=Santa Fe, N.M.|publisher=Fontanel Books|page=25|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/angelupmysleeve0000scot/page/25/mode/1up|isbn=0-9709048-7-8|passage=For high in the brightest tower of Light Castle, one thing shone still brighter—the Princess of Light! She came from before all the '''befores''', from a place that is no place. Not fire. Not water. Not air. Not earth. No place. Neither solid, nor liquid, nor gas. Nothing to speak of.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2003|author=Cynn Chadwick|chapter=16|title=Cat Rising|location=Binghamton, N.Y.|publisher=[[w:Harrington Park Press|Alice Street Editions]]|page=236|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/catrising00chad/page/236/mode/1up|isbn=1-56023-408-3|passage=The packing that took all week to finish had also taken her mind off Mike. Less and less she found herself weeping. Her focus was on the ''nexts''. There was little time now to think about all the '''''befores'''''. Today would put an end to the last leftover one.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2011|author=w:Mary E. Pearson|chapter=74|title=The Fox Inheritance|series=Jenna Fox Chronicles|seriesvolume=2|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher=w:Henry Holt and Company|page=285|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=2h0-VfzYFLYC&pg=PA285|isbn=978-0-8050-8829-8|passage=We talk about all the '''befores'''. The stupid things we did. The funny things. The times she made us laugh.}}
# {{lb|en|rare}} A [[previous]] [[form]] or [[instance]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1999|month=March|author=w:Julia Vinograd|title=The Homeless|journal=[[w:Street Spirit (newspaper)|Street Spirit]]|volume=5|issue=3|location=San Francisco, Calif.|publisher=w:American Friends Service Committee|page=13|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/cuig_000182/page/13/mode/1up|oclc=33465744|passage=A big wind blew all their '''befores''' away. Impacted teeth grew over their names. Even the lines in their hands unraveled, these are the lines they stand in to ask for their hands back.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2006|author=Walee {{quote-gloss|pseudonym}}|chapter=I Never Can Say Goodbye|title=What’s on the Menu? All of Me! Literary Entrees Prepared by Walee|location=Lincoln, Neb.|publisher=w:iUniverse|section=chapter 3|page=55|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/isbn_9780595390410/page/55/mode/1up|isbn=978-0-595-39041-0|passage=I guess I should have known from all the '''befores''' / that when it’s all said and done / I don’t want to be / I won’t stand to be / I refuse to be / anything but YOURS}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2015|author=w:Sarah Pinborough|chapter=14|title=w:The Death House|location=London|publisher=[[w:Victor Gollancz Ltd|Gollancz]]|page=160|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/deathhouse0000pinb/page/160/mode/1up|isbn=978 0 575 09690 5|passage=They were chatting and laughing and it made my heart hurt. They were getting out. Returning to whatever their '''''befores''''' were. They didn’t even glance back at the house as they climbed into the waiting vehicles.}}

